Description: Wayland: hand a window drawn once per eye over as the desktop's depth
 .
 Stereo KWin shows depth inside a surface when a toolkit draws the surface's
 elements once per eye and hands the two views over side by side. A raster
 window whose backing store holds both eyes, the window one view wide (the
 widgets' repaint manager sets the window's _q_stereo_pair for it), is now
 declared with kde_stereo_content_v1 as a full side-by-side pair and marked
 with kde_stereo_depth_v1 as the desktop's own depth rather than stereo
 content, with the commit that carries it, both views damaged; when the
 window is painted once again the declaration is withdrawn.
 .
 The objects are made only for a window that is ever painted as a pair, so
 every other window talks to the compositor as before. They need version 3
 of kde_stereo_content_manager_v1; the protocol is carried in
 3rdparty/wayland/protocols/kde-stereo-content. The state lives beside the
 display and the window rather than in them, which keeps their layouts.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
